aurants, Southern","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","review_id":"FXSVRBGz7YUEvsBX-YJPng","date":"2020-12-16T23:19:27","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9546329379081726,"text_excerpt":"Went for happy hour/dinner! Great deals on drinks and $1 chargrilled oysters (soooo tasty!). We got seated outside and the area/ambiance was very lovely. Felt safely distanced from other customers. Our server was very friendly and pleasant. The gumbo and crawfish pasta were also very delicious. We also ordered the shrimp jalapeno popper and the crawfish beignets. The beignets tasted good but were very heavy, not sure I'd order it again. I'd recommend this place to anyone visiting New Orleans, especially the happy hour! I would go back just for the oysters and drinks."},{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","review_id":"LXRR0LW83THlM9j6KVSs4Q","date":"2012-09-01T13:56:46","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.946797251701355,"text_excerpt":"Started the night with cold beer and fresh oysters. Moved on to fresh chilli batter fish and ended with a very good cup of coffee! This was a surprise, came here on a Monday night and the place was slow. Came here with a co- worker and met a customer. We sat in front of the oyster bar/ drink bar and started off with some beers and raw oysters. Our server was not only shucking oysters, but kept us laughing with great jokes. Later we order our food and the fish was fresh and the chili batter was something I had not tasted before. I'm looking forward to a return visit when I go to NOLA, again in Sept. Almost forgot, try a cup of their seafood gumbo, delicious!!!!"},{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","review_id":"NoNCWXsL6q8bFKZ-TBYpXA","date":"2014-11-21T19:42:35","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9458125233650208,"text_excerpt":"I had and would recommend the Grand Oysters, Shrimp and Grits, and Lavender Margarita. The margarita was delicious although I didn't taste the lavender syrup, it was refreshing. The shrimp and grits were rich and creamy, and had andouille sausage in them. It was the first time my friend had shrimp and grits and I'm glad she tried them at a place that did them justice. The Grand Oysters were baked with breadcrumbs and other seasonings. They were absolutely delicious. We only ordered half dozen, but I should have gone back for the other 6. Everything was simple but well done. The service was typically southern- attentive and warm. The decor was bright and open. Definitely a good go-to place..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","photo_id":"ZaGmNbnTv8hEX4HewYGUsQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/ZaGmNbnTv8hEX4HewYGUsQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8371343612670898},{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","photo_id":"O2CVqb3WRIz3PH5YDeDtRg","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/O2CVqb3WRIz3PH5YDeDtRg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8330790996551514},{"business_id":"zSqTndm5Alq9dW1PyzbdTA","photo_id":"rSSe9